To implement the `is_torch_oom` function in C#, we need to determine if a given exception is a PyTorch out-of-memory (OOM) error. This involves checking if the exception is an instance of `System.Runtime.InteropServices.ExternalException` (which is the base class for CUDA OOM errors in .NET when using Python interoperability) or a `System.Exception` with a specific message indicating an out-of-memory error.

Here's how you can implement this function in C#:

```csharp
using System;

public class OOMChecker
{
    public static bool IsTorchOOM(Exception exc)
    {
        if (exc is ExternalException externalException)
        {
            // Check if the exception is a CUDA OOM error
            return externalException.Message.Contains("CUDA out of memory");
        }
        else if (exc is Exception exception)
        {
            // Check for a general RuntimeError with a specific OOM message
            string message = exception.Message;
            return message.Contains("CUDA out of memory") || message.Contains("MPS backend out of memory");
        }
        return false;
    }
}

